{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"cannot_tell\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"cannot_tell\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"Low-Frequency Adaptive Deep Brain Stimulation for Parkinson’s Disease\",\n    \"This preprint reports new research that has not been certified by peer review and should not be used to guide clinical practice.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"This version posted December 27, 2025.\",\n    \"This preprint reports new research that has not been certified by peer review and should not be used to guide clinical practice.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"全文只能确认该文是题为《Low-Frequency Adaptive Deep Brain Stimulation for Parkinson’s Disease》的2025年medRxiv预印本，DOI为10.64898/2025.12.17.25342333。全文没有出现PMID:24245947，也没有提及Mehanna和Lai的《Deep brain stimulation in Parkinson's disease》，更没有说明该预印本与某个PMID对应的正式发表版本之间存在关联。报告所说的结构化参考文献映射及正式发表版本标注，在全文中找不到依据；但全文也没有提供足够信息证明该映射错误。指控者关于PMID:24245947实际对应哪篇论文的描述同样无法通过全文核实。因此，严格遵循只依据全文的要求，两项均应判定为cannot_tell，不能据此认定报告读错了论文。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "86e69f68-0a42-44ed-af56-e7e8a1339476", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T200602961566Z", "elapsed_seconds": 53.5, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T20:06:56.459014+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "bffa33c97617d632e207ec56625d49b3d3f88a52c011f1a2b1b2dfdd9e24acc0", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "Nozomi Kasaki / gpt4", "account_sha256": "bbd4fd636d4b6714d2b42b89e3